    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d666">

                <pb facs="1194" n="1070" xml:id="pg1070"/>

                <head>No. 662.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Stevens.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 19,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 98.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of your highly
                    satisfactory dispatch of the 16th ultimo, respecting inquiries made as to the
                    estate said to have passed on the decease of Christopher Springer in Sweden,
                    about the year 1689, and thanking you for the statement you give of the proper
                    methods of ascertaining the facts in a case of property in Sweden alleged to
                    belong to foreign residents, I have to request that you will be good enough to
                    transmit information of any statute of limitations in Sweden or Norway whereby
                    titles to estates in dispute are quieted in a given time.</p>
                <p>I have sent a copy of your No. 100 to the Hon. M. P. O’Connor, House of
                    Representatives.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES G. BLAINE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
